{%- comment -%}
  "Get 10% off your first order" — the second of the two storefront pop-ups.

  Its settings now live in the booking admin's Popup tab (shop metafield
  booking_app.popup_settings, the `offer` half), NOT in Theme settings, so the
  two cards are controlled from one place. The script decides for itself
  whether to show, and it ships off.

  `settings.saf_newsletter_enabled` is therefore no longer read. It is left in
  the theme rather than removed, so nothing that referenced it breaks; changing
  it now does nothing.

  The basket is skipped outright — a visitor part-way through paying is never
  interrupted. Checkout is hosted by Shopify and never renders theme snippets,
  so it excludes itself. Which kind of page this is comes from
  window.__saPopupPage, set by snippets/lead-popup.liquid.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless request.page_type == 'cart' -%}
  {%- assign _nl_api = shop.metafields.booking_app.quiz_api_url | default: 'https://sa-art-fair-admin.vercel.app' -%}
  <script>
    window.__safNewsletter = { apiUrl: {{ _nl_api | json }} };
  </script>
  <script src="{{ 'newsletter-popup.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
{%- endunless -%}
